# Quorum configuration — every setting the backend reads, with no values.
#
# The backend reads `server/.env` (relative to `server/`, where uvicorn runs).
# Copy this file there and uncomment the lines you are actually setting: every
# setting below has a working default in `server/app/config.py`, and an empty
# value overrides it rather than falling back to it — which for the numeric
# ones stops the server from starting. Real environment variables win over the
# file, which is how the test suites override it.
#
# The web app has one setting of its own, in `web/.env.local`:
#
#   BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8000
#
# Next.js rewrites `/api/*` and `/llm/*` to it, so the browser only ever talks
# to the Next.js origin and the session cookie stays first-party.

# --- Voice (Agora Conversational AI) ------------------------------------------
# Leave the app id and certificate empty to run the interview in text mode.

# Agora project app id.
# AGORA_APP_ID=
# Agora app certificate; mints RTC/RTM tokens and authenticates the REST calls.
# AGORA_APP_CERTIFICATE=
# Deepgram speech-to-text model, on Agora's managed credentials.
# AGORA_ASR_MODEL=
# MiniMax text-to-speech model, on Agora's managed credentials.
# AGORA_TTS_MODEL=
# MiniMax voice for the whole panel; roles change the label, never the voice.
# AGORA_TTS_VOICE_ID=

# --- The endpoint Agora calls back ---------------------------------------------

# Public HTTPS origin of this backend, no trailing slash. Agora's agent runs in
# Agora's cloud and must be able to reach it, so in development this is a tunnel.
# CUSTOM_LLM_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=
# HMAC key for the per-interview bearer token on /llm/{id}/chat/completions.
# CUSTOM_LLM_AUTH_SECRET=

# --- Model ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# `openai` for a real OpenAI-compatible endpoint, `scripted` for the deterministic
# test double used by the automated tests. Never `scripted` in a real interview.
# LLM_PROVIDER=
# Base URL of the OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
# LLM_BASE_URL=
# API key for that endpoint.
# LLM_API_KEY=
# Model identifier; recorded on every assessment so a report says what wrote it.
# LLM_MODEL=

# --- Execution -----------------------------------------------------------------

# E2B API key, for the sandbox every candidate run executes in.
# E2B_API_KEY=
# `e2b` for the isolated sandbox, `local` for a subprocess (development and tests).
# EXECUTOR=

# --- Sessions and storage -------------------------------------------------------

# HMAC key for capability-token hashes. Rotating it invalidates every open link.
# SESSION_SECRET=
# SQLite database file, relative to `server/`.
# DATABASE_PATH=
# Directory the candidate's code snapshots are written to, relative to `server/`.
# SNAPSHOT_DIR=
# Comma-separated origins allowed to call the API and to send cookies with it.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
# Days an interview is kept before the hourly sweep deletes everything about it.
# RETENTION_DAYS=

# --- Limits ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Wall-clock seconds a single run of the checks may take before it is a timeout.
# RUN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=
# Bytes of captured stdout/stderr kept from a run.
# RUN_OUTPUT_CAP_BYTES=
# Total bytes of editable source a candidate may save in one snapshot.
# SOURCE_LIMIT_BYTES=
# Runs one interview may start, replays included.
# MAX_RUNS_PER_INTERVIEW=
# Session length cap in minutes, excluding paused time.
# SESSION_CAP_MINUTES=

# --- Scenario and pacing ----------------------------------------------------------

# Directory holding the scenarios, relative to `server/`.
# SCENARIO_DIR=
# Which scenario an interview runs.
# SCENARIO_ID=
# Quiet seconds after a run completes before the panel raises it unprompted.
# FOLLOW_UP_DELAY_SECONDS=
